      "official_mark_scheme_text": "M1: Resolve vertically with four terms (allow $T_A,T_B$, sign errors, or missing $g$): $500+T\\cos45^\\circ+T\\cos45^\\circ-100g=0$.\nA1: Require $T_A=T_B=T$; allow the sign-reversed force convention.\nA1: $T=354$ N; allow $250\\sqrt2$ or $500/\\sqrt2$. If the sign-reversed equation gives $T=-354$, allow if the magnitude 354 is stated; A0 if $T_A,T_B$ are different.\nAlternative 1, perpendicular to a strut: M1 resolve three terms; A1 $T_A$ (or $T_B$)$+500\\cos45^\\circ=100g\\cos45^\\circ$ (allow sign-reversed); A1 $T_A=T_B=354$.\nAlternative 2, triangle of forces: M1 use Pythagoras/trigonometry with four terms; A1 $T_A^2+T_B^2=(100g-500)^2$ plus symmetry, or equivalent sine/cosine relation; A1 $T_A=T_B=354$.\nAlternative 3, Lami: M1 attempt Lami; A1 $(100g-500)/\\sin90^\\circ=T_A/\\sin135^\\circ$ (or listed sign-equivalent forms); A1 $T_A=T_B=354$.\nPrinted total: 3.",
